(* Beginning of Notebook Content *)
Notebook[{
Cell["Osculating Orbital Elements", "Title"],

Cell["\<\
The method of osculating geodesics follows an orbit under a force as a \
sequence of geodesics: at each moment the orbit is the geodesic with the same \
position and velocity, and the force changes which geodesic that is. This \
package integrates those equations for bound orbits in Kerr spacetime, and \
also drives inspirals with fluxes, orbit-averaged rates of change of the \
elements. It builds on KerrGeodesics.\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<OsculatingOrbitalElements`\>\"", "]"}]], "Input"],

Cell["An inspiral", "Subsection"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["OsculatingInspiral",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:OsculatingOrbitalElements/ref/OsculatingInspiral"]], 
  "InlineFormula"],
 " takes an Association of parameters: the spin a, the small mass ratio \
\[Epsilon], the initial semi-latus rectum p, eccentricity e and inclination x \
= cos \[Iota], and a force, a flux or both. Here gas drag drives the inspiral \
until it reaches the separatrix:"
}], "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"inspiral", "=", 
  RowBox[{"OsculatingInspiral", "[", 
   RowBox[{"Association", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\"\<a\>\"", "\[Rule]", "0.9`"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<\[Epsilon]\>\"", "\[Rule]", 
      FractionBox["1", 
       SuperscriptBox["10", "3"]]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<p\>\"", "\[Rule]", "8"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<e\>\"", "\[Rule]", "0.3`"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<x\>\"", "\[Rule]", "0.6`"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Force\>\"", "\[Rule]", 
      RowBox[{"ForceModel", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<GasDrag\>\"", ",", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<Coefficient\>\"", "\[Rule]", 
         FractionBox["1", 
          SuperscriptBox["10", "4"]]}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}]], "Input"],

